From: FiyeroT <me@fiyero.xyz>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 07:50:13 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 149/174] clashapi: an external UI that fails to unpack leaves
 the one served

The download of the external UI (at the start into an empty directory, and on
POST /upgrade/ui) unpacked the archive over the files served and, when that
failed, removed everything in the directory: an upgrade on a router with too
little free space ("no space left on device" halfway through the 4.6 MB of
Yacd-meta) left the dashboard empty until it was downloaded again.

The archive is now unpacked into a directory of its own inside the external
UI directory, on the same file system whether that is a mount point or a
symbolic link, and its files replace the others only when all of them are
there; they are moved, not copied. A failure removes only what was unpacked.
An archive with no files, or with a path that leads out of the directory, is
refused instead of written; one with a single file at its root no longer
makes the unpacking panic.
